      "evaluation": {
        "acceptance_conditions": [
          "Freeze one primary relation family q_* and one surface specification Σ_* before any generator or dataset is created.",
          "Define generator constraints for positive, negative, relation-preserving, and relation-breaking instances while generating no data.",
          "Freeze split sizes and held-out surface-domain law.",
          "Freeze F_S, F_G, and F_R model-class contracts without implementing them.",
          "Freeze M, δ_min, C_break, κ_min, leakage thresholds, uncertainty procedure, model-selection policy, compute/search budget policy, stopping law, and replication law.",
          "Preserve BENCHMARK_INVALID and UNDERDETERMINED as genuine outcomes.",
          "Keep RGR-05, benchmark generation, model implementation, empirical execution, Elemental hypothesis, MAIA change, and deployment closed."
        ],
        "falsification_conditions": [
          "Surface variables can predict q_* beyond the frozen leakage tolerance by construction.",
          "Positive and relation-breaking counterfactuals cannot be paired while preserving the frozen surface realization.",
          "A comparator receives privileged information unavailable under the information-access contract.",
          "The benchmark encodes one candidate geometry as ground truth rather than testing the formalism-neutral H-RT1 claim.",
          "Any metric, threshold, split, or model-selection criterion remains open to post-result adjustment."
        ],
        "stop_conditions": [
